{
  "slug": "js_modules_import",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 235,
  "url": "/js/js_modules_import.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Modules Import",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Modules Import"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Import"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can import modules in two ways, based on if they are\nnamed exports or default exports."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import { name, age } from \"./person.js\";",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import message from \"./message.js\";",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Named Imports"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Named imports match named exports in a module."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "They let you import one or more explicitly named variables or functions from a module."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You must use the exact names enclosed in curly { } braces:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import { name, age } from \"./person.js\";",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "import { add, subtract, PI } from './math.js';",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_modules1"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Named Import Rules"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Import names must match export names:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import { addd } from './math.js'; // ❌ Error (name mismatch)",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can import multiple items at once:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import { add, PI } from './math.js';",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can rename them using as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import { add as addition } from './math.js';",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Default Import"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Default import is the way to import the primary exported value from a module -\nthe one that was exported using export default."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Defalt imports are the counterpart to default exports."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can give a default export any name you like, during import, without using curly braces:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import text from \"./message.js\";",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import message from \"./message.js\";",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_modules_import"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Default Import Rules"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Default import imports single default exports"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import message from \"./message.js\";",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "There is no required name. Renaming is allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import text from \"./message.js\";",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Default + Named Import"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A module can provide one main function plus some helpers:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "export default function parse() { ... }\n\nexport function validate() { ... }\n\nexport function format() { ... }",
      "caption": "Module File"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "import parse, { validate, format } from './parser.js';",
      "caption": "Module File"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Importing All"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can import all named exports from a module as a single object using the * syntax."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Import all named exports from person.js\n\nimport * as person from \"./person.js\";",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Import all named exports from math.js\n\nimport * as math from \"./math.js\";",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_modules4"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Default Import vs Named"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Feature", "Default Import", "Named Import"],
        ["Typical use case", "One main feature per module", "Multiple features"],
        ["Matches export name?", "No (you choose)", "Yes (must match)"],
        ["Can rename freely?", "Always", "Only with as"],
        ["Export count", "Only one default export allowed", "Multiple exports allowed"]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
